		{"id":"cc86db0f02126de8","type":"text","text":"**Anthropomorphism\n\n> **Anthropomorphism is the attribution of human characteristics, emotions, or intentions to non-human entities.**","x":-515,"y":-582,"width":250,"height":200},
		{"id":"65784488fdf5e481","type":"text","text":"Anthropomorphism","x":-515,"y":-682,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"ad422125380e17c7","type":"text","text":"==is the way things appear to us as meaningful wholes within a situation.== We always perceive something against a background, through our bodily relationship with the world.","x":531,"y":69,"width":263,"height":226},
		{"id":"7bcebeab279ce4a4","type":"text","text":" perception\n %%知觉经验%%\n ","x":370,"y":94,"width":125,"height":50,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"eefb220eac930e03","type":"text","text":"==how we experience meaningful things in context.==","x":538,"y":364,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"acfe250eb4968fbb","type":"text","text":"When looking at the same flickering light source, one animal may see a steady light, while another may see it flicker.","x":538,"y":484,"width":250,"height":142},
		{"id":"d9402705278e19cf","type":"text","text":"is the body’s contact with sensory qualities, such as colour, sound, and texture. It is never completely isolated or meaningless. For example, the red of a carpet is experienced through its texture, lighting, and surroundings","x":538,"y":-297,"width":256,"height":220},
		{"id":"501d16f18dd3e970","type":"text","text":" different perception of time","x":38,"y":-36,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"5"},
